QuestGuidance.Register("en",321,{
[10241]="70062DD1\n1\tCollect holly berries from huorns or wood-trolls in Western Eregion (total: 6)\tHolly berries can sometimes be found on the huorns and wood-trolls that stalk Western Eregion.\n2\tBring the holly berries to Lornel at Idhobel\tLornel is by the camp-fire at Idhobel.\n",
[10242]="70034C1F\n1\tListen to Cyneberg recount a story of Thrymm's past\tCyneberg is impressed with your actions and how you helped Forlaw in these gloomy times. She would like to tell you about how you remind her of Thrymm.\n2\tSpeak with Gárwig\tGárwig also enjoyed listening to the tale of Thrymm defending Forlaw. It is rare to hear stories of hope these days.\n",
[10243]="700154CF\n1\tCollect dwarf sheet-music (total: 6)\tThe dwarf-bard's sheet music has been spread throughout the Orc-camps in Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm. With the failure of his plan, Hamall wishes to raise the spirits of his fellow dwarves in Jazârgund. He believes collecting the songs of old lost by the maddened bard will help achieve this goal.\n2\tBring the sheet-music to Hamall\030Collect Sheet-music (total: 6)\tHamall is at Jazârgund, west of Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm. Hamall's spirits will be greatly raised by the ancient dwarf-songs you recovered.\n",
[10244]="70057388\n1\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe Ungoladan chieftain, Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms, bars your path deeper into the Remmorchant.\n2\tDefeat Thossulun the Massive\tThossulun the Massive, daughter of Shelob and Queen of all gredbyg, must be defeated to stem the tide of insects harassing your allies.\n3\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious scheme to you. You must defeat him and his Bloodless captain, Zabothak, to prevent Shelob from being unleashed!\n4\tDefeat Shelob the Great, Last Child of Ungoliant\tThe last challenge is finally upon you: defeat Ungwetári herself!\n",
[10245]="70057389\n1\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe Ungoladan chieftain, Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms, bars your path deeper into the Remmorchant.\n2\tDefeat Thossulun the Massive\tThossulun the Massive, daughter of Shelob and Queen of all gredbyg, must be defeated to stem the tide of insects harassing your allies.\n3\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious scheme to you. You must defeat him and his Bloodless captain, Zabothak, to prevent Shelob from being unleashed!\n4\tDefeat Shelob the Great, Last Child of Ungoliant\tThe last challenge is finally upon you: defeat Ungwetári herself!\n",
[10246]="7005738A\n1\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe Ungoladan chieftain, Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms, bars your path deeper into the Remmorchant.\n2\tDefeat Thossulun the Massive\tThossulun the Massive, daughter of Shelob and Queen of all gredbyg, must be defeated to stem the tide of insects harassing your allies.\n3\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious scheme to you. You must defeat him and his Bloodless captain, Zabothak, to prevent Shelob from being unleashed!\n4\tDefeat Shelob the Great, Last Child of Ungoliant\tThe last challenge is finally upon you: defeat Ungwetári herself!\n",
[10247]="700579A5\n1\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe Ungoladan chieftain, Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms, bars your path deeper into the Remmorchant.\n2\tDefeat Thossulun the Massive\tThossulun the Massive, daughter of Shelob and Queen of all gredbyg, must be defeated to stem the tide of insects harassing your allies.\n3\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious scheme to you. You must defeat him and his Bloodless captain, Zabothak, to prevent Shelob from being unleashed!\n4\tDefeat Shelob the Great, Last Child of Ungoliant\tThe last challenge is finally upon you: defeat Ungwetári herself!\n",
[10248]="700579A6\n1\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe Ungoladan chieftain, Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms, bars your path deeper into the Remmorchant.\n2\tDefeat Thossulun the Massive\tThossulun the Massive, daughter of Shelob and Queen of all gredbyg, must be defeated to stem the tide of insects harassing your allies.\n3\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious scheme to you. You must defeat him and his Bloodless captain, Zabothak, to prevent Shelob from being unleashed!\n4\tDefeat Shelob the Great, Last Child of Ungoliant\tThe last challenge is finally upon you: defeat Ungwetári herself!\n",
[10249]="7005507B\n1\tDestroy befouled artifacts in Bâr Maenath (total: 10)\tBâr Maenath can be found in the Circle of Death. You have discovered a number of befouled artifacts in Bâr Maenath. You should destroy them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many befouled artifacts in Bâr Maenath.\n",
[10250]="7004941F\n1\tDefeat trolls and Olog-hai at Dâr Mauzur\tTrolls and Olog-hai can be found at Dâr Mauzur. You should defeat as many trolls and Olog-hai as possible.\n2\tDefeat trolls at Dâr Mauzur (total: 6)\030Defeat Olog-hai at Dâr Mauzur (total: 4)\tTrolls and Olog-hai can be found at Dâr Mauzur. You should defeat as many trolls and Olog-hai as possible.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many trolls and Olog-hai at Dâr Mauzur.\n",
[10251]="700529CD\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tCollect Woodmen belongings (total: 10)\tWoodmen belongings can be found scattered around Shathur-munzu. You should collect Woodmen belongings.\n3\tTalk to Garsind\tGarsind, the chieftain of Arhaim, would be interested in these belongings. You should talk to Garsind in Arhaim.\n",
[10252]="70028C8E\n1\tFind the item at the first patrol point\tThe items Ardwyn has requested lie along a path through the valley to the west of Forthbrond. Ardwyn has asked you to recover the belongings of his missing patrol.\n2\tFind the item at the second patrol point\tThe items Ardwyn has requested lie along a path through the vallet to the west of Forthbrond. Ardwyn has asked you to recover the belongings of his missing patrol.\n3\tFind the item at the third patrol point\tThe items Ardwyn has requested lie along a path through the vallet to the west of Forthbrond. Ardwyn has asked you to recover the belongings of his missing patrol.\n4\tBring the recovered items to Ardwyn at Forthbrond\tArdwyn is at Forthbrond, east of the valley. You should deliver the items you recovered to Ardwyn.\n",
[10253]="7002282F\n1\tDefeat wights (total: 10)\tThese creatures move among many of the barrows in the southern reaches of the Lich Bluffs. Mincham has asked you to seek out and defeat any wights that you might encounter.\n2\tTalk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs\tMincham is located south and slightly east of the large Gondorian ruins in the Lich Bluffs. You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have defeated many wights.\n",
[10254]="700173B2\n1\tBring the Mithril Bits to Sigir at Anazârmekhem\030Collect mithril-bits (total: 24)\tThe Forges of Khazad-dûm lie to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. Sigir asked you to collect bits of mithril from the forces of the Enemy now inhabiting the Forges of Khazad-dûm.\n",
[10255]="70047CEE\n1\tCollect Éothéod artifacts (total: 20)\tCollect Éothéod artifacts from the many ruins in the Noman-lands.\n2\tReturn to Éomer King\tÉomer King can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien. You should return to Éomer King with the artifacts you found.\n",
[10256]="70053F23\n1\tRemove spoiled food in Díngarth (total: 10)\tSpoiled food can be found in Díngarth. You should remove any spoiled food found in Díngarth.\n2\tTalk to Ohtar\tOhtar can be found in Díngarth. You should talk to Ohtar.\n",
[10257]="7001A4A8\n1\tDefeat Taughâsh archers at Ashúrz Maufulug (total: 4)\tOrc-archers can be found patrolling the outskirts of Ashúrz Maufulug, south and a little west from Echad Glamodúd. Glamodúd has asked you to defeat the Orc-archers who defend Ashúrz Maufulug.\n2\tTalk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd\tGlamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north and a little east from Ashúrz Maufulug. You should return to Glamodúd with news of your victory.\n",
[10258]="7001A63D\n1\tPlant the mallorn seedling in Sâd Meryrn\tSâd Meryrn can be found due south of Nífdir's camp, but you should strike north and west to reach the glade. Nífdir has asked you to plant the mallorn seedling in Sâd Meryrn.\n2\tTalk to Nenedhel at Estolad Mernael\tNenedhel awaits news of Nífdir's endeavour at Estolad Mernael, east of Nífdir's encampment. You should speak with Nenedhel and inform him that Nífdir's task is complete.\n",
[10259]="7004DCE1\n1\tSalute Dale merchants (total: 5)\030Calm angry shoppers (total: 3)\030Congratulate happy shoppers (total: 3)\030Assist indecisive shoppers (total: 3)\030Visit the Upper Markets, north\030Visit the Upper Markets, south\030Visit the Jolly Bell tavern\030Visit the Lower Markets, west\030Visit the Lower Markets, central\030Visit the Lower Markets, south\tYou should visit and be seen at the various market areas and tavern in Dale, salute merchants, congratulate happy shoppers, assist indecisive shoppers, and calm angry shoppers on the way.\n2\tReturn to Rótha\tYou should return to Rótha, who can be found inside the Great-keep in Dale.\n",
[10260]="7004147B\n1\tOrders can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir. Gorroch has asked you to recover orders from the Corsairs to aid the warriors of Dor-en-Ernil in preparing for a renewed assault on Linhir.\t\n2\tBring the notes you found to Gorroch\tGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir. You have recovered two pages of the Corsairs' orders and should now return them to Gorroch.\n3\tSearch for the last page of the Corsairs' orders\tThe last page of orders can likely be found on a Corsair captain in Hata Khezrat. Gorroch has asked you to seek one last page of orders from the Corsairs at Hata Khezrat.\n4\tRead the Corsair orders\tThe orders can be found in your inventory. You have skilfully taken the orders from a drunk Corsair and should now read them.\n5\tTalk to Gorroch\tGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir. You have found and read the last of the Corsairs' orders, and should now tell Gorroch of what you have learned.\n",
[10261]="7006211C\n1\tPlant fake orders (quantity: see journal)\tSaeloril has asked you sneak the forged orders into places where they will be found in Nímbarth. Nímbarth is located in south-east Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Saeloril\tYou should let Saeloril know that you have planted fake orders. Saeloril is near Nímbarth in Cardolan.\n",
[10262]="7002E3D7\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Edgal\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (total: 15)\tblah blah\n",
[10263]="70037C86\n1\tDefend labourers as they repair and crank the portcullis ([see journal]/30)\tThe broken portcullis mechanism must be repaired so that the passageway can be sealed off and the intruders denied passage. The men working to repair the portcullis will require protection from serious harm if they are to succeed in their task. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10264]="70062CE5\n1\tGather chopped wood (total: 4)\tPonta Gochelgar has asked you to cut down trees from which to make planks to repair the bridges. Trees can be found along the river below the cliffs of Glyn Helyg.\n2\tBring the wood to Ponta\tYou should bring the wood to Ponta. Ponta Gochelgar is in Glyn Helyg.\n",
[10265]="70025A7C\n1\tCollect bundles of rope (total: 6)\030Collect pieces of driftwood (total: 4)\030Collect small flywheels (total: 2)\030Collect oil-pouches (total: 3)\tBundles of rope, pieces of driftwood, small flywheels, and oil pouches can be found along the banks of the Baranduin. Sardan asked you to gather some supplies to help fix a catapult.\n2\tBring the items to Cudhaer near the colossus\tCudhaer is on a bluff overlooking the colossus from the south. Cudhaer will be eager to use these supplies to repair the catapult.\n",
[10266]="7002718C\n1\tCollect broken tools (total: 8)\030Collect iron ore (total: 8)\tIron ore and broken tools can be found within the Barnavon Mine. Bervun asked you to enter the Barnavon Mine and collect iron ore and broken tools.\n2\tReforge broken tools\tThe forge is outside the Barnavon Mine. Bervun asked you to bring the iron ore and broken tools to the forge and repair the tools.\n3\tBring the restored tools to Bervun at the mine\tBervun is near the forge outside the Barnavon Mine. You should bring the restored tools to Bervun.\n",
[10267]="700166EE\n1\tRepair sluice-boxes (total: 10)\030Collect Pry Bar\tBroken sluice-boxes can be found at the bases of the elevated tracks throughout the Redhorn Lodes, south-east of the Orc-watch. Auti asked you to venture into the Redhorn Lodes and repair the sluice-boxes the White Hand Orcs had broken. They do not serve an immediate value, but once the mining operations are restored, they will be used to filter the ore.\n2\tReturn the pry bar to Auti at the Orc-watch\tAuti is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Redhorn Lodes. Auti will be pleased to hear the sluice boxes have been repaired.\n",
[10268]="7001E98D\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Ânghum-maudhûl (total: 15)\030Collect grim tokens (total: 10)\tÂnghum-maudhûl lies to the south-east of Mithechad. Harchador has asked you to journey to Ânhum-maudhûl to defeat the Orcs and collect the grim tokens they bear.\n2\tTalk to Harchador at Mithechad\tHarchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl. You should return to Harchador with news of your success.\n",
[10269]="700266E1\n1\tTalk to Bróin and travel to Mirror Halls of Lumul-nar\tThe entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering. Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.\n2\tTalk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[10270]="700266EB\n1\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.\n2\tTalk to Bósi and travel to Water-works of Nalâ-dûm\tThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria. Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy.\n3\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi. You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[10271]="700077DD\n1\tBring Redweed's report to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is at the Boar Fountain in Bree, north and west of Staddle. Watcher Redweed has asked you to deliver his message to Second-watcher Heathstraw.\n",
[10272]="70021D49\n1\tSpeak with Captain Brackenbrook\tNed Pruner has asked you to report your findings to Captain Brackenbrook.\n",
})
